      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is acceptable with regard to the comment in l.3021. If PermissionMonitor#startMonitoring fails to complete within 3 seconds, this happily continues execution with MultipathPolicyTracker.start() before PermissionMonitor is done, so it silently breaks the system !\n\nToday this method waits for PermissionMonitor#start, no matter how long it takes. So if you wait forever here, you\u0027re not changing the logic.\n\nI understand why you\u0027d want to establish a time limit for this to run, and that\u0027s fine, but you need to be VERY, VERY sure it will never be exceeded. Have you tested that this runs under 3 seconds on the slowest OEM device with hundreds of apps installed ?",
